# Playwright test structure

This repo has no sample specs. Before writing tests, read `.cursor/skills/write-playwright-tests/SKILL.md` and follow it.

## Where files go

- Logged-out UI: `tests/guest/<feature>.spec.ts` (project `guest-*`)
- Logged-in UI: `tests/e2e/<feature>.spec.ts` (project `e2e-*`)
- API: `tests/api/<feature>.spec.ts` (project `api`)
- Pages: `src/pages/<name>.page.ts`, extending `BasePage`
- Widgets used by more than one page: `src/components/<name>.component.ts`
- API clients: `src/api/<name>.client.ts`
- Response schemas: `src/api/schemas/<name>.schema.ts`
- Data-driven cases: `test-data/<name>.json`, loaded with `readJson`
- Saved login only: `tests/setup/auth.setup.ts` → `playwright/.auth/*.json`

## Spec rules

- Import `{ test, expect }` from `src/fixtures/test.fixture.ts`. Do not import `test` from `@playwright/test` in a spec.
- Call `meta()` from `src/utils/allure.ts` as the first line inside every test.
- Tag with `{ tag: ['@smoke'] }`, `@regression`, `@a11y`, or `@quarantine`. CI skips `@quarantine`.
- Navigate with a relative path. `baseURL` is `env.baseUrl`.
- Assert in the spec. Page methods perform actions and return state.
- Register each page as a fixture in `src/fixtures/test.fixture.ts` before a spec uses it.
- Locator order: `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByPlaceholder`, then `getByTestId`. `getByTestId` matches `data-testid`.
- Confirm locators on the live site. Do not invent selectors, use `waitForTimeout`, commit `test.only`, or hardcode an absolute URL.
